WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:07.270
Speaker 1: Hey, David, why don't Republicans
focus on policy instead of culture war issues?

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.830
Wouldn't it be better for them electorally?

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.720
I don't know that it would be.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.869
And the reason that I say that is it's not
clear to me that Republicans actually have

00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:20.939
the support to win on the issues.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:27.539
If what what was it that Donald Trump did
that prior Republicans didn't do that essentially

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:30.400
gave Trump the victory in 2016.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:39.410
It was that he ran a campaign based on cultural
issues and personal attacks and fears about

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:46.260
communism, socialism, Hillary, et cetera,
where his voters didn't actually have to evaluate

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.120
policy and say, does the policy actually sound
good to me?

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.260
Some examples where the Republican Party,
if they were to run on policy, would have

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.760
a problem.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.310
Abortion is still used to raise a lot of money
by Republican candidates.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.650
But the truth is that the American public
is more in favor of abortion being legal in

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:07.770
most cases than it has at any time in the
Roe v. Wade era.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:14.740
So if Republicans really made abortion a bigger
issue, it might not be so good for them.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.350
If you look at the Republican perspective
on.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:23.219
Taxation, when you really get down to it,
I've said a lot of bad things about the populist

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:28.539
movement and how they can bamboozle people,
but one of the things that the more populist

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:35.359
Republican base has gone towards is to be
more hostile to tax plans that are just good

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:36.359
for rich people.

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:38.649
Now, Trump still passed one that is mostly
that.

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:43.850
But because policy was so secondary and the
cultural issues were more important, Trump

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.619
was able to achieve an electorate that really
doesn't care very much what his policy is.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:51.709
Most of the things he promised he was never
going to be able to do and it didn't even

00:01:51.709 --> 00:01:52.709
matter.

00:01:52.709 --> 00:01:53.709
No one actually held him accountable.

00:01:53.709 --> 00:01:57.009
And ultimately, what brought Trump down was
his mishandling of the covid pandemic.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:03.369
I maintain that if the covid pandemic hadn't
happened and because Trump mishandled it.

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:04.369
Right, there's the idea.

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:05.560
Well, Trump could have handled it well.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.259
And one, yeah, Trump was not going to handle
it well.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:12.700
If Trump didn't end up having to mishandle
covid, he almost certainly would have been

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.000
reelected.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.780
And to me, when you say, why doesn't the Republican
Party run on policy, it seems to me it's actually

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.840
better for them electorally to run on.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.600
These cultural issues were against critical
race theory.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.770
Nobody can even define it.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:29.850
These people barely know what it is, but it
gets so much oxygen.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.860
Think about the coverage of critical race
theory on Fox News over the last three to

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.110
four months.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.400
And then think of how it fires up the base
and it spreads.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.470
I mean, these memes spread like wildfire.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.470
Money is raised.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:45.100
I'm coming out in opposition of critical race
theory and schools donate to me.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.920
Imagine if the entire time it had been about
like tax policy, they would not have gotten

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.800
the attention that they did.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.920
And so to me, it actually seems, you know,
same thing with we're against communism and

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.920
socialism.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.270
Joe Biden's making us a communist nation.

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.790
You ask these people, what is communism?

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.490
They have no idea.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:07.490
And this allows them to continue moving forward
without ever really having to be accountable

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.680
for bad policy by just not talking about policy.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:16.850
I actually am increasingly of the mindset
that Republicans do better right now by talking

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:21.790
about the cultural issues than they do by
actually switching over to policy.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:27.190
Check out my segment from earlier this week,
whether a culture war is even winnable, because

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.460
that's another factor that the left has to
consider.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:35.280
But I don't think that I think it's disgusting
in terms of the debasement of American political

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.810
discussion that there's one party that doesn't
even pretend to care about policy that's really

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.780
bad for the country.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:46.830
But I think it's probably, in a sense, the
better choice for the Republican Party in

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:52.500
terms of winning elections, because they have
a constituency that wants to just fight and

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.480
yell and scream and cheer about cultural issues.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.250
And they don't really want to deal with policy
in any serious way.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.320
That's why Trump won in 2016.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.380
Were it not for covid, he would have won in
2020 as well.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.170
Send me your thoughts if you disagree with
me.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.510
I do want to hear from you.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.340
We have a great bonus show for you today.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:13.380
